hanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":53410,"endPos":61387,"startLine":974,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":1111,"endLineOffset":5,"length":7978}]}]},{"comment":"The `getTierPreference` method in `QueryRewriteContext` should be static if it does not rely on any instance-specific data. Since the method is now static and used across different contexts, ensure that all usages are updated accordingly to call the static method directly from `QueryRewriteContext`.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java-3010:3732-16060:17012","promptId":"#PBB5M","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3010,"endPos":3732,"startLine":84,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":99,"endLineOffset":9,"length":723}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":16060,"endPos":17012,"startLine":414,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":435,"endLineOffset":5,"length":953}]}]},{"comment":"The changes in these diffs introduce a new parameter `tier` to the `createCoordinatorContext` method. Ensure that all test cases and usage scenarios of this method account for the new parameter. The default value provided in `#9TP8A` is an empty string, which should be handled appropriately in the context where it\u0027s used.","nodes":[{"id":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java-test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java-28243:28598,28611:28721-28533:28594","promptId":"#9TP8A","srcPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java","dstPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":28243,"endPos":28598,"startLine":628,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":633,"endLineOffset":14,"length":356},{"pos":28611,"endPos":28721,"startLine":634,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":634,"endLineOffset":122,"length":111}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":28533,"endPos":28594,"startLine":637,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":637,"endLineOffset":73,"length":62}]},{"id":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java-test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java--28614:29251","promptId":"#P4JY0","srcPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java","dstPath":"test/framework/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/test/AbstractBuilderTestCase.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":28614,"endPos":29251,"startLine":640,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":648,"endLineOffset":9,"length":638}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":60,"line":60,"comment_lines":["[][60]"],"review_comment":["perhaps make it super clear that the range info will only have a value for read only indices, because those are the only indices for which that info is populated in the cluster state","I believe read-only indices is a superset of where we actually have this optimization available - i.e. only for fully and partially mounted indices ?\r\nI believe the comment is accurate if my assumption is correct (i.e. hot/warm indices don\u0027t have this optimization, cold/frozen ones - fully/partially mounted ones - do) but happy to clarify further if you have a better suggestion? "],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/CoordinatorRewriteContextProvider.java","id":35577,"created_at":"2024-10-23T18:56:25Z","original_position":9,"side":"RIGHT","position":9,"submitted_on_commit":"de96932eeae689053d9dc52d99950bd6fa0ae2bf","diff_hunk":"@@ -52,6 +52,12 @@ public CoordinatorRewriteContext getCoordinatorRewriteContext(Index index) {\n             return null;\n         }\n         DateFieldRangeInfo dateFieldRangeInfo \u003d mappingSupplier.apply(index);\n+        // we\u0027ve now added a coordinator rewrite based on the _tier field so the requirement\n+        // for the timestamps fields to be present is artificial (we could do a coordinator\n+        // rewrite only based on the _tier field) and we might decide to remove this artificial\n+        // limitation to enable coordinator rewrites based on _tier for hot and warm indices\n+        // (currently the _tier coordinator rewrite is only available for mounted and partially mounted\n+        // indices)","submitted_line":60},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":426,"line":421,"comment_lines":["[][421]"],"review_comment":["I find it surprising that how we read the index setting here differs from how we read it above in CoordinatorRewriteContextProvider. Why is that? Reading the tier from index settings should require the same logic in those two places?","We\u0027ve had performance issues in the past with parsing the tier preference from the settings. We now have a version of the `IndexMetadata` that does the parsing and caches the result for the lifetime of the `IndexMetadata`. \r\nSince the `CoordinatorRewriteContextProvider` has access to the `IndexMetadata` I preferred to take this route rather than re-parsing the setting."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java","id":35578,"created_at":"2024-10-23T18:58:26Z","original_position":30,"side":"RIGHT","position":25,"submitted_on_commit":"de96932eeae689053d9dc52d99950bd6fa0ae2bf","diff_hunk":"@@ -407,4 +410,27 @@ public ResolvedIndices getResolvedIndices() {\n     public PointInTimeBuilder getPointInTimeBuilder() {\n         return pit;\n     }\n+\n+    /**\n+     * Retrieve the first tier preference from the index setting. If the setting is not\n+     * present, then return null.\n+     */\n+    @Nullable\n+    public static String getTierPreference(QueryRewriteContext context) {\n+        if (context instanceof CoordinatorRewriteContext) {\n+            String tier \u003d ((CoordinatorRewriteContext) context).tier();\n+            // dominant branch first (tier preference is configured)\n+            return tier.isEmpty() \u003d\u003d false ? tier : null;\n+        }\n+        Settings settings \u003d context.getIndexSettings().getSettings();\n+        String value \u003d DataTier.TIER_PREFERENCE_SETTING.get(settings);","submitted_line":426},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The `getTierPreference` method in `QueryRewriteContext` should be static if it does not rely on any instance-specific data. Since the method is now static and used across different contexts, ensure that all usages are updated accordingly to call the static method directly from `QueryRewriteContext`.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java-3010:3732-16060:17012","promptId":"#PBB5M","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/query/QueryRewriteContext.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3010,"endPos":3732,"startLine":84,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":99,"endLineOffset":9,"length":723}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":16060,"endPos":17012,"startLine":414,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":435,"endLineOffset":5,"length":953}]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":1,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":14,"uncoveredMatchable":19,"timing":92301,"tokensIn":25089,"tokensOut":779}